   "id": 632616,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"7\" type=\"1\">\n    <li>Which scenario could describe the graph?       <p><br><img alt=\"GRAPH OF AN INCREASING EXPONENTIAL FUNCTION WITH A \\(y\\)-intercepts OF 10 AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS (1, 20) AND (2, 40).\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"314\" src=\"exercises/media/984ed32adb153c9f.jpg\" width=\"326\">;</p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1225086,
     "content_html": "A population of bacteria starts with 200 and decays by a factor of <span data-math=\"\\frac12\">\\frac12</span> every hour."
    },
    {
     "id": 1225087,
     "content_html": "A population of bacteria increases by a factor of 10 every hour and starts with 2 bacteria."
    },
    {
     "id": 1225088,
     "content_html": "A savings account starts with $200 and decays by a factor of <span data-math=\"\\frac12\">\\frac12</span> each month."
    },
    {
     "id": 1225089,
     "content_html": "A population of bacteria doubles every hour and starts with 10 bacteria."
    }
